    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), who headlines our strategy as the premier play. His matchup against the right-handed Irvin provides a massive 14% boost due to favorable platoon splits, and his elite sprint speed against a pitcher with a slow delivery makes him a primary target for stolen base production. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (77.68) and **Yordan Alvarez** (76.93) are high-efficiency anchors; **Junior Caminero** benefits from a park factor boost and an advantageous order position, while **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start despite the L/L matchup, buoyed by an elite 0.465 xwOBA and wind conditions expected to carry the ball out.\n\nStrategic efficiency remains the focus in the secondary slots, where **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) and **Christian Yelich** (65.65) leverage significant platoon advantages against right-handed starters to secure their spots. **Trea Turner** (65.12) continues to be essential for his speed-based value, with his score reinforced by a slow-delivery pitcher who mitigates the risk of a sub-optimal park factor. The most difficult decision rested on the bench, where **Carson Benge** (50.14) fell just short of a start. While he projects reasonably well against the lefty P\u00e9rez, he was squeezed out by the sheer volume of high-scoring, high-leverage platoon plays elsewhere in our outfield and utility slots. \n\nManagers should remain vigilant as we await final confirmation on several lineups, including **Gary Sanchez**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Trea Turner**, **Junior Caminero**, **Yordan Alvarez**, **Nelson Velazquez**, **Kyle Schwarber**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Christian Yelich**. While the raw data supports these starts, volatility in batting order positions remains our primary operational risk. Furthermore, we are monitoring **Hector Rodriguez** (45.58) on the bench, whose marginal score is further suppressed by a 33% rain risk; we will hold him in reserve to protect our game caps unless weather reports clear significantly before first pitch.",
